en  i'm the founder of keller works naturals  we're a sensitive skin care company we  make products for people with eczema and  allergies  nine years ago my little boy elliot  developed a rash on his face  and it quickly spread all over his body  we took him to about 14 different  doctors  and found out that it was caused by  eczema  from his allergies so i looked and  looked for products to help maintain his  skin  and i couldn't find anything free of his  allergens  which led me to create my own skin care  line within two weeks  the the rash had completely cleared  everyone around us  noticed and they said what did you use  and where do i get it  that's when i knew i had a business and  there was a need and i could fill it  thank you so much drew for the  opportunity to be on the show  thank you kristen and  kendra do you have a question for  kristen  yes so what does your competitive  landscape look like  who are you competing against and what  makes your product stand out from theirs  my competitors that i usually focus on  are companies like  cerave but the leg up that i have on  that  is the fact that we're all natural and  we use no chemicals whatsoever in our  product  i know you think that the what separates  you is some of just what's in the  product what separates you  is you your story your experience  your relatability to other mothers and  parents  you have that over any one of your  competitors that are in drug stores  across america  so celebrate that absolutely that's  excellent advice  thank you so much erica amber  jennifer it's your turn what is your  pitch and what is your story  okay so we are the sisters of colonel's  national popcorn  our story starts a long time ago when we  were kids  our parents always got us the popcorn  tins for christmas you know the caramel  cheddar and butter  and we just gobble it up every every  holiday  season and so it just became a family  tradition so  we fast forward some years and um it was  christmas break of